    "body": "Industrial output help U.S. railroads steel themselves against increasing demand and show some mettle amid uncertain economic conditions.\nFor the week ending Oct. 17, total U.S. weekly rail traffic was 540,135 carloads and intermodal units, up 8.5% from the same week a year ago, according to the Association of American Railroads .\nCarloads totaled 232,120 units, up 3.5%, and intermodal volume of 308,015 containers and trailers was 12.6% better y/y.\nNine of the 10 carload commodity groups posted an increase compared with the same week in 2025.\n(Chart: AAR)\nMetallic ores and metals used in steelmaking and other production led all gainers, up 14.5%. Domestic raw-steel production increased 4.1% from the previous week, the latest American Iron and Steel Institute figures show. Petroleum and related products improved 8.8%, and grain was ahead 7%.\nNonmetallic minerals such as sand and stone was the only category to retreat, down 3.2% y/y.\nFor the first 41 weeks of 2026, U.S. railroads posted cumulative volume of 9,374,717 carloads, an increase of 2.7%, and 11,687,964 intermodal units, up 4.6% from 2025. Total combined traffic for the first 41 weeks of 2026 was 21,062,681 carloads and intermodal units, an improvement of 3.7% y/y.\nNorth American rail volume for the week on nine reporting U.S., Canadian and Mexican railroads totaled 339,034 carloads, a gain of 3.2%, and 392,681 intermodal units, up 10.8% y/y. Total combined weekly rail traffic in North America was 731,715 carloads and intermodal units, up 7.2%. North American rail volume for the first 41 weeks of 2026 was 28,828,693 carloads and intermodal units, up 3.2% compared with 2025.\nSubscribe to FreightWaves’ Rail e-newsletter and get the latest insights on rail freight right in your inbox.\nRead more articles by Stuart Chirls here .\nRead more:\nFirst look: Union Pacific earnings\nFirst look: Norfolk Southern earnings\nCSX profit jumps on volume and revenue growth\nNew York short line wins $11.2 million federal rail grant\nAutonomous railcar technology earns $16M federal grant\nUpcoming FreightWaves Events\nCompliance\nBrokerage Compliance Symposium\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nAwards\nF3 Awards Dinner\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nOctober 26, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nFreightTech\nF3: Future of Freight Festival\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nOctober 27, 2026 – October 28, 2026\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nRegister Now\nCompliance Brokerage Compliance Symposium Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe day before F3. Every compliance issue you face - fraud exposure, carrier liability, FMCSA rules, cargo theft, insurance gaps - navigated by attorneys and operators defining best practices in a changing industry.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nAwards F3 Awards Dinner Oct 26 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nThe night before F3. FreightTech100 companies honored. FreightTech 25 and Shipper of Choice winners revealed live. Cocktail reception into dinner and live music - 300 industry leaders in one purpose-built room.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now\nFreightTech F3: Future of Freight Festival Oct 27 – Oct 28 • The Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN\nIndustry-defining keynotes, rapid-fire technology demos, and industry leaders networking in experiences across Chattanooga - plus the inaugural F3 Awards Dinner featuring the FreightTech and Shipper of Choice reveals.\nThe Signal at Chattanooga Choo Choo • Chattanooga, TN Register Now",
